  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1217 PM CDT Wed Aug 26 2026\n\nH500 high pressure is still forecast to transition east and\nheights will expand across the southern US in the extended. Later\nnext week, there are still differing solutions as to how far east\nthe high pressure center anchors itself. Some models like the \noperational ECMWF suggest the high sets up over the Mid Atlantic \nand keeps favorable southwestern steering flow over our CWA. This \nwill allow precipitation to still fall in our northern and \nwestern zones throughout the week. However, if the high sets up \nfurther west across the deep south and portions of the central \nCONUS, a much drier outlook can be expected for the next 7 days. \nPoP trends have decreased in the latest NBM forecast, so the \npotential for the drier outcome seems to be favored at this time.\n\nOverall trends holds for hot temperatures to return to the entire\nFA. Highs next week currently range between 100 to 107. Heat \nproduct issuance is expected to return possibly as early as this \nweekend, but this will mainly be for Palo Duro Canyon.\n\nRangel",
